      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Food allergy presents in two distinct forms: acute allergy with symptoms of anaphylactic type (acute urticaria, Quincke's oedema, anaphylactic shock); chronic allergy with symptoms of atopy (atopic dermatitis, asthma, rhinitis). Care in a rural environment includes the feature of distancing the care structure."},
